On Thu, 08 Jan 2004 09:13:40 -0800, Micha Pringle wrote:

> Has anyone considered adding sound to nethack? For example, if you
> were hungry, a nice clip from the old Guantlet "Wizard needs food,
> badly" might be appropriate.

If you're using one of the tiled gui nethacks, make sure you've also
installed the nethack-sounds package for your machine Frankly, I don't
play with sounds, but they're available.

And the "{Wizard|Elf|Valkyrie} needs food badly" message really is in
there. Adding the voices from the Atari game, though, would obviously
involve some hairy licensing. If you really really want them, remember
that this is an open source game, and you're free to add patches that
nobody else has. :)

> Has anyone considered making a "note" feature, basically just a text
> area accessible within a game so a player can make notes about that
> game, like "level 2 has a vault", "Arch-Lich on level 8 of GM" etc?

Easy enough to do that with a simple text editor or a pad and paper,
rather than try to code an editor in to the game. (Do you really want to
see vi-vs-emacs wars between the devteam? ;) And you can always engrave
those kinds of notes on the stairwells, eg "DANGER: ArchLich below."

